---
system: sys-19-billing-subscription
flow_id: dunning-past-due
surface: cron
spec_anchor: /software/systems/19-billing-subscription#dunning-past-due
actors: [BillingService, Stripe, PostgreSQL, SES, FCM, NotificationService, EventBridge]
apis:
  - POST /v1/billing/payment-method/update
externals: [Stripe, SES, FCM]
queues: [EventBridge, SQS]
failure_paths:
  - stripe_charge_failed_again
  - customer_unreachable
  - grace_period_expired
  - payment_method_not_updated
idempotency: sweep idempotent on (subscription_id, run_date); SetupIntent confirmation is Stripe-idempotent
retry: at 3-day boundaries; Stripe handles within-day retries internally
timeout: sweep batch 10min budget; per-subscription 5s p99
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant EventBridge
    participant BillingService
    participant Stripe
    participant PostgreSQL
    participant NotificationService
    participant SES
    participant FCM

    EventBridge->>BillingService: billing.dunning.sweep (daily cron)
    BillingService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT subscriptions WHERE state='past_due' ORDER BY past_due_since ASC
    PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: batch of past_due subscriptions

    loop for each past_due subscription
        BillingService->>BillingService: check idempotency — skip if already swept today (subscription_id, run_date)
        BillingService->>Stripe: POST /v1/invoices/{latest_invoice_id}/pay (retry charge attempt)
        alt stripe_charge_failed_again
            Stripe-->>BillingService: payment_intent failed — decline code
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE subscriptions SET retry_attempts=retry_attempts+1 WHERE id=?
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT EXTRACT(DAY FROM now() - past_due_since) AS days_in_past_due
            PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: days_in_past_due
            alt grace_period_expired (days_in_past_due >= 7)
                Note over BillingService: hard expiry — cancel and revoke entitlements
                BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE subscriptions SET state='cancelled', canceled_at=now()
                BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE content_entitlements SET revoked_at=now() WHERE household_id=? AND revoked_at IS NULL
                BillingService->>NotificationService: enqueue entitlement_revoked notification (sys-10)
                NotificationService-)SES: send entitlement_revoked email
                NotificationService-)FCM: push entitlement_revoked notification
            else days_in_past_due between 3 and 6 (second reminder)
                BillingService->>NotificationService: enqueue dunning_reminder_2 {subscription_id, days_in_past_due}
                NotificationService-)SES: send dunning reminder #2 email
                NotificationService-)FCM: push dunning reminder #2 notification
            else days_in_past_due < 3 (first reminder)
                BillingService->>NotificationService: enqueue dunning_reminder_1 {subscription_id, days_in_past_due}
                NotificationService-)SES: send dunning reminder #1 email
                NotificationService-)FCM: push dunning reminder #1 notification
            end
        else charge_succeeded
            Stripe-->>BillingService: payment_intent succeeded
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE subscriptions SET state='active', past_due_since=NULL, retry_attempts=0
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE content_entitlements SET revoked_at=NULL WHERE household_id=? (restore if soft-revoked)
            BillingService->>NotificationService: enqueue payment_recovered notification (sys-10)
            NotificationService-)FCM: push payment_recovered notification
        end
    end

    Note over BillingService,PostgreSQL: sweep budget 10min — per-subscription p99 5s — idempotent on (subscription_id, run_date)

    Note over BillingService,FCM: parent reactivation path (separate mobile surface)
    Note over BillingService: parent taps "Update Payment Method" in app → mobile calls POST /v1/billing/payment-method/update
    BillingService->>Stripe: POST /v1/setup_intents {customer_id, usage: 'off_session', metadata.subscription_id}
    Stripe-->>BillingService: {client_secret: seti_..., id: si_...}
    BillingService-->>BillingService: return {setup_intent_client_secret} to ParentApp (not shown — mobile-surface step)
    Note over BillingService: ParentApp completes SetupIntent in Stripe SDK (Stripe-idempotent)
    Note over BillingService: on setup_intent.succeeded webhook → BillingService attaches new PaymentMethod + retries charge immediately
    alt payment_method_not_updated (setup_intent cancelled or timed out)
        Note over BillingService: subscription remains past_due — next daily sweep will retry
    else new_payment_method_success
        BillingService->>Stripe: POST /v1/invoices/{latest_invoice_id}/pay
        Stripe-->>BillingService: payment_intent succeeded
        BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE subscriptions SET state='active', past_due_since=NULL
        BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE content_entitlements SET revoked_at=NULL WHERE household_id=? (restore if soft-revoked)
        BillingService->>NotificationService: enqueue payment_recovered notification
        NotificationService-)FCM: push payment_recovered
    end

    Note over EventBridge,FCM: queues: EventBridge (cron trigger), SQS (notification delivery via sys-10)
